regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.txt:86:| `dev_mk48txx.c`: 118 | 1 | **I1:** ordinary MK48T08 RAM bytes reach default | **E1:** correct the RAM boundary |
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.txt:136:**Title:** `DEVICE_ACCESS(mk48txx) misclassifies MK48T08 NVRAM bytes as unsupported registers and terminates ordinary RAM accesses.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.txt:138:The grep anchor is [`DEVICE_ACCESS(mk48txx)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_mk48txx.c:76); the exit is at **118**. The actual [MVME187 constructor](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/machines/machine_mvme88k.c:114) explicitly attaches an **MK48T08**.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.txt:140:The range bypass leaves bank-relative positions **0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8** entering the switch. Its sole case handles **8**, `MK48TXX_ICSR`. Thus the eight positions **0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7** reach default. An ordinary NVRAM scan can encounter them. The [included register header](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/mk48txxreg.h:43) distinguishes the older part’s RAM from the extra register bank on newer variants.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.txt:142:Choose **accept the value using existing storage**. Extend the RAM bypass through the byte preceding `MK48TXX_ICSR`: **one boundary-condition change**. The existing RAM read/write path and `reg[]` storage then handle these bytes. The switch receives only its implemented CSR case; its default exit becomes unreachable. Removing that dead diagnostic tail is optional cleanup, not necessary to close the live defect.
