regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:32527:The strongest fixes are reads that already have backing storage. Maple DMAADDR and XScale INTEN compute the return value, then exit. The MK48T08 NVRAM handler has a similar issue: its range check sends eight RAM bytes into the unimplemented-register branch. That boundary correction belongs near the top of the effort list.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:32637:64: - [dev_mk48txx.c](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_mk48txx.c:118), [dev_mvme187.c](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_mvme187.c:80), [dev_vme.c](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:143): unimplemented mapped accesses; MVME187 also **90**.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:34498:The final batch has seven ready-to-file entries, led by Maple readback, XScale readback, and the MK48T08 RAM boundary. The source census leaves 76 unowned runtime error exits in 24 files. The report separates those from disabled attachments, dead branches, and internal guards whose failure has not been established, with a disposition and an existing test carrier for each proposed entry.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:34500:VERDICT: 1. Maple `MAPLE_DMAADDR` readback; 2. XScale `INTEN` readback; 3. MK48T08 NVRAM boundary.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:34585:| `dev_mk48txx.c`: 118 | 1 | **I1:** ordinary MK48T08 RAM bytes reach default | **E1:** correct the RAM boundary |
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:34635:**Title:** `DEVICE_ACCESS(mk48txx) misclassifies MK48T08 NVRAM bytes as unsupported registers and terminates ordinary RAM accesses.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:34637:The grep anchor is [`DEVICE_ACCESS(mk48txx)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_mk48txx.c:76); the exit is at **118**. The actual [MVME187 constructor](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/machines/machine_mvme88k.c:114) explicitly attaches an **MK48T08**.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:34639:The range bypass leaves bank-relative positions **0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8** entering the switch. Its sole case handles **8**, `MK48TXX_ICSR`. Thus the eight positions **0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7** reach default. An ordinary NVRAM scan can encounter them. The [included register header](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/mk48txxreg.h:43) distinguishes the older part’s RAM from the extra register bank on newer variants.
regress\artifacts\queuetriage\codex_exitaudit_20260910.err:34641:Choose **accept the value using existing storage**. Extend the RAM bypass through the byte preceding `MK48TXX_ICSR`: **one boundary-condition change**. The existing RAM read/write path and `reg[]` storage then handle these bytes. The switch receives only its implemented CSR case; its default exit becomes unreachable. Removing that dead diagnostic tail is optional cleanup, not necessary to close the live defect.
